// ============================================================
// 22. INTERPRETATION NOTES
// ============================================================
//
// delta_elevation_mean_m = urban_mean_m - rural_mean_m
//
// If delta_elevation_mean_m > 0:
//   urban area is higher than rural area.
//
// If delta_elevation_mean_m < 0:
//   urban area is lower than rural area.
//
// lapse_rate_bias_mean_C = delta_elevation_mean_m × -0.0065
//
// Example:
//   urban is 100 m lower than rural
//   delta = -100 m
//   bias = -100 × -0.0065 = +0.65 °C
//
// That means apparent urban warming may be enhanced partly because
// the urban zone is lower than the rural reference.
//
// The point-sample export can be used for:
//   - urban/rural elevation boxplots
//   - violin plots
//   - DEM uncertainty plots
//   - elevation distribution overlap analysis
//
// ============================================================
